^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-07-20] observe — repo pins typescript ~5.9.3; TS 6 (bridge) and TS 7 (native Go) are both released. TS 7 has no stable programmatic API until ~7.1.
 >>[2026-07-20] observe — tsconfig.base.json still sets baseUrl (deprecated in 6, hard error in 7). types not explicit (6/7 default types to []).
 >>[2026-07-20] observe — extensions/vscode-spw pins typescript ^5.2.0 while root uses ~5.9.3 — pin drift.
 >>[2026-07-20] observe — package uses @typescript-eslint/parser ^8.57.2; dual-install will be required if default tsc becomes 7 before eslint supports native API.
 >>[2026-07-20] decide — ladder order is non-skippable: prep on 5.9 → 6 clean → dual 7+6 API → optional default flip. Speed claims require perf-audit baselines.
 >>[2026-07-20] decide — never land ignoreDeprecations:6.0 on mainline; treat deprecations as rung A/B work.
 >>[2026-07-20] taste — version story should be as clear as Spw sigils: one command, one compiler, one documented fallback.
}

